Cell["\<\
Notice that L[r] +  constant is also a solution to the lapse equation. So we \
can choose a constant such that at the boundary of the star, L[r] is equal to \
its Schwarzschild value for a given mass. Thus to obtain the correct \
solution, we choose an arbitrary value for L at r=0, and then obtain the \
correct solution once we have computed \[Rho] and m\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.000304046771308*^9},ExpressionUUID->"f526568f-7ccf-4d33-a309-\
1eb61e4e6352"],

